[]{#sec:ILP label="sec:ILP"} We now turn to our main focus. Associated with $\operatorname{LP}(A,b,c)$ is the integer linear program $$\label{eq:ILP}
  \begin{array}{ll}
    \max & c^tx\\
    \textrm{s.t.} & Ax \le b \, , \ x \in {\mathbb{Z}}^n  \, ,
  \end{array}$$ which we denote as $\operatorname{ILP}(A,b,c)$. Throughout we make the same assumptions as above: the linear program $\operatorname{LP}(A,b,c)$ is feasible, the matrix $A$ does not have any zero rows, and the inequalities bijectively correspond to the hyperplane arrangement ${\mathscr{H}}(A,b)$; see Remark [\[rem:scale\]](#rem:scal
